"The Onset and the System are the powered backdrop of the world."
"In the Onset, powers began surfacing across the world a few years before the present."
"In the Onset, ordinary people woke up changed."
"The System is a flat, indifferent overlay that registers everyone with attributes."
"The System has no personality and no voice."
"Growth is theft, and only theft."
"There are no levels and no experience."
"The only way anyone grows is by Acquisition."
"Every stat point Pearl gains is an auditable theft, carved off a specific named victim."
"Ordinary people carry whatever spread the System registered on them; they do not climb."
"There are two steal categories, attributes and powers, and no skill category."
"An attribute steal takes a +10% slice of one of the victim's six attributes."
"The six attributes are Might, Vitality, Celerity, Acuity, Will and Allure."
"The System scores perceptiveness as Acuity, senses and precision, not as a separate skill."
"An attribute steal works on anyone, since everyone has attributes."
"A power steal takes one of the victim's powers."
"A power can be stolen only from an awakened victim, never from someone who has none."
"A stolen power's output is multiplied by the thief's Will."
"The reading is flat and indifferent; the relish is entirely Pearl's."
"Powers are rare."
"Most people never awaken."
"The overwhelming majority of people carry no power at all."
"A minority, the awakened, carry a single Onset power layered on top of their attributes."
"The System registers the power an awakened person carries."
"The rarity of powers shapes how Pearl hunts."
"Early in her career Pearl's victims are unpowered humans, beautiful and gifted."
"Every theft Pearl banks early in her career is an attribute slice."
"Dove was an unpowered victim from whom Pearl took an attribute slice."
"When Pearl kills an awakened victim, a power becomes available to take."
